              "text": "Depending on your location and context, **Chase Capital Services** typically refers to one of two things: the lessor name used on **U.S. auto leases** managed by Chase Auto, or an **independent financial services firm in India**. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Auto Leases and Vehicle Titles (United States)\nIf you are looking at a car title, registration, or lease agreement and see the name **Chase Capital Services**, this refers to **Chase Auto** (the automotive financing division of JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A.).\n\n* **Why is it on your title?** Chase Auto is the private label financier and lessor for several major vehicle brands (historically or currently including Mazda, Subaru, Jaguar Land Rover, Maserati, and Aston Martin). Because a leased car is owned by the bank until you buy it out, Chase Capital Services is officially listed on the title and registration as the **owner/lessor**.\n* **Handling a Lease Buyout:** If you decide to purchase your leased vehicle, you must contact Chase Auto to request a payoff quote. Once you pay the buyout amount, Chase will send you the physical title (still listing Chase Capital Services) along with a **Lien Release** and/or **Power of Attorney (POA)**. You must take these documents to your local DMV to officially transfer the title into your name.\n* **Moving Out of State:** If you move to another state while leasing, your new state's DMV will require proof of ownership to register the car. You will need to contact Chase Auto to request they send a copy of the title and a Power of Attorney directly to your new state\u2019s DMV so you can register the vehicle.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chase Capital Services Private Limited (India)\nIf you are looking for a business entity in India, **Chase Capital Services (P) Ltd.** is an independent financial consulting firm incorporated in May 1997. \n\n* **Location:** Headquartered in Chandigarh / Mohali, Punjab, India.\n* **Services:** This company is engaged in project consultancy, debt syndication, securitization services, currency and commodities trading, and corporate advisory. \n* *Note: This company is entirely independent and is **not affiliated** with the American multinational bank JPMorgan Chase & Co.*\n\n---\n\n### 3. JPMorgan Chase Corporate & Capital Services\nIf you are looking for corporate investment or business funding solutions from JPMorgan Chase & Co. directly, you may be referring to:\n* **Chase for Business / Commercial Banking:** Chase provides business loans, merchant services, lines of credit, and cash management solutions for small-to-midsize businesses.\n* **J.P. Morgan Investment Banking:** For larger corporations, J.P. Morgan manages corporate financing, debt and equity capital markets, M&A advisory, and private capital placement.",
